      "essay": "Jio Platforms will open its IPO for public subscription on October 21 and close on October 23, with a potential listing on October 28, according to reports. The offering targets a valuation of roughly $106 billion and could raise about INR 30.0 billion, making it India's largest IPO to date. The issue consists of fresh shares intended partly to repay borrowings, and Reliance held 66.43 percent of Jio Platforms as of March 31, 2026.\n\nThe financials show improving leverage and growth. Jio Platforms' net leverage fell from 0.88 times in fiscal 2024 to 0.36 times in fiscal 2026. Revenue from operations rose from INR 110.0 billion to INR 147.0 billion over the same period, while profit after tax increased from INR 21.423 billion to INR 30.049 billion. Its telecom arm had 524.4 million customers as of March 2026.\n\nJefferies raised its model portfolio weight for Reliance Industries to 7.50 percent as the IPO approaches. Reliance reported first-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue of INR 340.257 billion, up 24.50 percent year over year, and profit after tax of INR 23.196 billion. For someone holding Jio Platforms, the IPO gives a public valuation for the digital business and a defined timetable, with anchor interest expected around October 19.",
